 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Snooping works because every cache hears every request on one bus. That stops working once there are dozens of cores, or several sockets. This video shows the alternative used in large machines: a directory."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Directory-based coherence"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the eight stages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Why snooping stops scaling, the directory idea, where it lives, and its states and messages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then the protocol at the home node, a full trace counted message by message, the storage cost, and an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[4..=7]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: what goes wrong with snooping? Every miss is broadcast, so every cache must see every request."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 8: why snooping stops scaling"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A bus carries one request at a time. Add cores, and the traffic grows, but the bus does not."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And every cache must look up its tags for every request, even though it almost never has the block."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "For a handful of cores, or one chip whose cores share an L3, that is fine."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "For many cores or many sockets, we want point-to-point messages, sent only to the caches that actually hold the block."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[4]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "broadcast does not scale"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "idea",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: the directory. For every block of memory it keeps two things."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 8: the directory idea"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "idea"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A state: is the block uncached, shared, or modified?"
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "idea[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And a set of sharers: one bit per processor, set if that processor's cache has a copy."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "idea[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Now a write needs no broadcast. The directory knows exactly which caches to invalidate."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "idea[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And because nothing is broadcast, the cores can be joined by any network: a mesh, a ring, a crossbar."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "idea[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "the directory knows who has each block"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "home",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: where does the directory live? One central directory would become the new bottleneck. So it is distributed along with memory."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 8: the home node"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "idea"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "dg"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Each node has a processor and cache, a slice of main memory, and the directory entries for that slice."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.c1"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.m1",
       "delay": 0.3
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The nodes talk over an interconnection network, not a bus."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.net"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.m1->net",
       "delay": 0.2
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.m2->net",
       "delay": 0.4
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.m3->net",
       "delay": 0.6
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "This gives three roles for every request."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "dg"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "nodes"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The local node: the one whose processor missed."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "nodes[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The home node: the one whose memory holds the block. The address alone decides it, so everyone knows where to ask."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "nodes[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And remote nodes: those whose caches hold a copy, as the owner or as sharers. Often a request touches all three."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "nodes[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "ask the home node · it knows the sharers"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "states",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4: the directory states mirror the cache states, but describe the block across all caches."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 4 of 8: states and messages"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "nodes"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "ds"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Uncached: no cache has it, and memory is current."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ds[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Shared: one or more caches have clean copies, and memory is still current."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ds[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Modified: exactly one cache, the owner, has written it. Memory is stale."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ds[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And these are the messages. The local node sends a read miss or a write miss to the home. The home answers with a data reply."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "ds"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "msg"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "msg[0..=1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "To take copies away, the home sends invalidate to a sharer."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "msg[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "To recover a dirty block, it sends the owner a fetch, or a fetch and invalidate. The owner answers with a data write-back."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "msg[3..=5]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "request · reply · invalidate · fetch · write-back"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "proto",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 5: what the home node does for each request. Uncached is the easy case: read or write, it just replies with the data. Two messages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 5 of 8: what the home does"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "msg"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "hp"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hp[0..=1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Shared, and a read miss: reply, and add the new processor to the sharers. Still two."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hp[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Shared, and a write miss: invalidate every other sharer, reply, and the writer becomes the only owner. Two messages plus one per sharer invalidated."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hp[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Modified, and a read miss: memory is stale. Fetch the block from the owner, who writes it back, then reply. Four messages, and the block ends shared by both."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hp[4]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Modified, and a write miss: fetch and invalidate the owner, then reply. Four messages, and the writer is the new owner."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hp[5]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Real machines also send acknowledgements for invalidations, so the writer knows when it is safe. Our counts leave those out, as the textbook does."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "U: 2 · S read: 2 · S write: 2 + sharers · M: 4"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trace",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 6: a trace. Four processors, one block X, homed on a separate node. The directory starts uncached."
     },
     "do": [
